# --- @fill: workplace prepositions an / op / bei --------------------------------
# This lesson's preposition drill: an = enclosed workplaces / industries,
# op = institutions / open places, bei = company names / persons.
# A1_05 already owns the basic op der Post / bei enger Bank set — these fills
# use A1.16's own workplace vocabulary instead. Distractors are the other two
# prepositions from the same three-way set.

@fill
@lu De Kach schafft [an] engem Restaurant.
@en The chef works [in] a restaurant.
@distractor-lu op
@distractor-lu bei
@distractor-lu mat
@distractor-en at
@distractor-en near
@distractor-en with

@fill
@lu D'Fotografin schafft [an] engem Studio.
@en The photographer works [in] a studio.
@distractor-lu op
@distractor-lu bei
@distractor-lu mat
@distractor-en at
@distractor-en near
@distractor-en with

@fill
@lu De Student studéiert [op] der Universitéit.
@en The student studies [at] the university.
@distractor-lu an
@distractor-lu bei
@distractor-lu mat
@distractor-en in
@distractor-en near
@distractor-en with

@fill
@lu Hie schafft [op] engem Büro.
@en He works [at] an office.
@distractor-lu an
@distractor-lu bei
@distractor-lu mat
@distractor-en in
@distractor-en near
@distractor-en with

@fill
@lu De Sekretär schafft [bei] engem Zänndokter.
@en The secretary works [at] a dentist's.
@distractor-lu an
@distractor-lu op
@distractor-lu mat
@distractor-en in
@distractor-en on
@distractor-en with

@fill
@lu Si schafft [bei] der BIL.
@en She works [at] the BIL.
@distractor-lu an
@distractor-lu op
@distractor-lu mat
@distractor-en in
@distractor-en on
@distractor-en with

# --- @fill: "als" for professions -----------------------------------------------
# The "schaffen als X" construction is the lesson's core pattern. Distractor "vu"
# tempts confusion with the parallel "X vu Beruff" frame; "mat" and "bei" are
# the other taught prepositions.

@fill
@lu Meng Mamm schafft [als] Doktesch an enger Praxis.
@en My mother works [as] a doctor at a practice.
@distractor-lu vu
@distractor-lu bei
@distractor-lu mat
@distractor-en from
@distractor-en near
@distractor-en with

@fill
@lu Hie schafft [als] Verkeefer an engem Supermarché.
@en He works [as] a salesman in a supermarket.
@distractor-lu vu
@distractor-lu bei
@distractor-lu mat
@distractor-en from
@distractor-en near
@distractor-en with

@fill
@lu Meng Schwëster schafft [als] Sekretärin op enger Bank.
@en My sister works [as] a secretary at a bank.
@distractor-lu vu
@distractor-lu bei
@distractor-lu mat
@distractor-en from
@distractor-en near
@distractor-en with

# --- @fill: verb conjugation — verkafen, schneiden ------------------------------
# Root-changing 2nd/3rd person singular: verkafen → verkeefs/verkeeft,
# schneiden → schneits/schneit. Distractors are wrong persons of the same verb.

@fill
@lu De Verkeefer [verkeeft] Wueren am Buttek.
@en The salesman [sells] goods at the shop.
@distractor-lu verkafen
@distractor-lu verkeefs
@distractor-lu verkaf
@distractor-en sell
@distractor-en sold
@distractor-en selling

@fill
@lu Du [verkeefs] Bicher an der Librairie.
@en You [sell] books at the bookstore.
@distractor-lu verkeeft
@distractor-lu verkafen
@distractor-lu verkaf
@distractor-en sells
@distractor-en sold
@distractor-en selling

@fill
@lu De Coiffeur [schneit] Hoer am Salon.
@en The hairdresser [cuts] hair at the salon.
@distractor-lu schneiden
@distractor-lu schneits
@distractor-lu geschnidden
@distractor-en cut
@distractor-en cutting
@distractor-en snipped

@fill
@lu Du [schneits] Brout an der Kichen.
@en You [cut] bread in the kitchen.
@distractor-lu schneit
@distractor-lu schneiden
@distractor-lu geschnidden
@distractor-en cuts
@distractor-en cutting
@distractor-en sliced

# --- @fill: "well" conjunction — verb goes to end -------------------------------
# The transcription (page 14) explicitly teaches "well" + verb-final word order.
# A comma before the blank satisfies the Eifeler-Regel adjacency rule.

@fill
@lu Si schafft vun doheem, [well] si Onlinecoursen gëtt.
@en She works from home [because] she gives online courses.
@distractor-lu wann
@distractor-lu obwuel
@distractor-lu datt
@distractor-en although
@distractor-en when
@distractor-en that

@fill
@lu Hie fiert mam Bus, [well] hie keen Auto huet.
@en He takes the bus [because] he has no car.
@distractor-lu wann
@distractor-lu obwuel
@distractor-lu datt
@distractor-en although
@distractor-en when
@distractor-en that

@fill
@lu Ech ruffen un, [well] d'Plaz nach fräi ass.
@en I am calling [because] the position is still available.
@distractor-lu wann
@distractor-lu obwuel
@distractor-lu datt
@distractor-en although
@distractor-en when
@distractor-en that

# --- @fill: "vu Beruff" pattern -------------------------------------------------
# The lesson's main question frame: "Wat bass du vu Beruff?" / "Ech sinn X vu
# Beruff." Distractors are other taught prepositions that could tempt confusion.

@fill
@lu Hien ass Architekt [vu] Beruff.
@en He is an architect [by] profession.
@distractor-lu als
@distractor-lu bei
@distractor-lu mat
@distractor-en as
@distractor-en at
@distractor-en with

@fill
@lu Si ass Coiffeuse [vu] Beruff.
@en She is a hairdresser [by] profession.
@distractor-lu als
@distractor-lu bei
@distractor-lu mat
@distractor-en as
@distractor-en at
@distractor-en with
